<report>
<line><title>Reference range/interval</title></line>
<line></line>
<table>
<tr><td>Sample name:</td><td><in>name</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample mean = </td><td><inu>mean</inu></td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample size n =</td><td><in>size</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Sample sd =</td><td><inu>sd</inu></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line><u>For normal data</u></line>
<line><in>qrr</in>% reference interval = <inu>lrr</inu> to <inu>urr</inu></line>
<line><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for lower range limit = <inu>lx_l</inu> to <inu>ux_l</inu></ci></line>
<line><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for upper range limit = <inu>lx_u</inu> to <inu>ux_u</inu></ci></line>
<block name="lognormal">
<line></line>
<line><u>For log-normal data</u></line>
<line><in>qrr</in>% reference interval = <inu>lrr_lognormal</inu> to <inu>urr_lognormal</inu></line>
<line><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for lower range limit = <inu>lx_l_lognormal</inu> to <inu>ux_l_lognormal</inu></ci></line>
<line><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for upper range limit = <inu>lx_u_lognormal</inu> to <inu>ux_u_lognormal</inu></ci></line>
</block>
<line></line>
<line><u>For any data</u></line>
<line>Quantile <inu>qx_any</inu> = <inu>qxv_any</inu></line>
<line><ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval <in>type</in> = <in>from_any</in> to <in>to_any</in></ci></line>
<line>Exact confidence level = <in>co_any</in></line>
<line></line>
<line>Quantile <inu>qx</inu> = <inu>qxv</inu></line>
<line><ci>Approximate <in>pc</in>% confidence interval <in>type</in> = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></line>
<line>Exact confidence level = <in>co</in></line>
</report>
